{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/634106-resurrection-numina-and-demon-template","id":634106,"title":"Resurrection Numina and Demon Template?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-20T17:58:46-07:00","id":634106,"title":"Resurrection Numina and Demon Template?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I've been re-reading the rules and I'm not sure what happens in this particular instance. Say a Demon dies and an Angel/Spirit uses the Ressurrection Numina on the corpse. Does it fail (e.g. is a Demon &quot;dead&quot; to begin with) or does the Demon get revived as a Stigmatic (e.g. the Demon loses its Major template for a Minor template)?<br /> <br /> The wording of the Numina is here:</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God Machine Chronicle, Pg 230</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">This Numen \u2014 only available to Rank 4+ angels and spirits of healing \u2014 raises the dead. The Numen costs 10 Essence to use and the activation roll is penalized by one die per day that the subject has been dead. Supernatural beings that have already died as part of their transformation \u2014 vampires, mummies and Sin-Eaters \u2014 can\u2019t be resurrected, nor can anyone who died of natural causes. Other supernatural beings lose their powers when resurrected. Mages become Sleepwalkers and werewolves, wolf-blooded. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 08-20-2015, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T19:28:46-07:00","id":634163,"title":"","content":"Demons are self-observers independent of their cover. Since what's being resurrected is the cover, I wouldn't rule that they lose - the demon just suddenly &quot;reconnects&quot; with the cover. I would roll a compromise with a good penalty - or make it so the cover wakes back up but the demon isn't part of it anymore. Your old cover is out there walking around actually being what you pretended to be, what do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T21:55:38-07:00","id":634249,"title":"","content":"Default answer, personally? I'd treat it as analogous to the Raise Dead Exploit. More versatile and simpler (though costly) to use, but most of the supernatural beings that can be targeted with this Numen have souls, or something resembling sufficiently soullike, to recover. A demon's Primum, the equivalent of its soul, doesn't simply leave the body on the death of the demon, but seems to gutter out, or at least move on swiftly somewhere it can't easily be recovered (for a relative value of &quot;easy&quot; when we're talking about miraculous Numina).<br /> <br /> Demons don't die separately from their Cover. The Cover is a psychic agglomeration of identifiers and relationships, a shell of perceptions directed at the demon; it has no will or awareness outside the demon's own. A work of sorcery or occult matrix that could make a separate willful being out of a demon's Cover might be possible, but it wouldn't be a work of resurrection, rather a work of creation ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> I could see a version of this Numen used by a powerful spirit, rather than an angel, possibly having a different effect, but it would probably be more complicated than either bringing the demon back fully intact or returning their consciousness as a stigmatic. I feel like the ability to escape the oppressive demands of Cover and compromise demands more than a single Numen, even one that has to be bargained out of rare and powerful gods of Shadow. Perhaps the demon's consciousness can't be returned without the god deigning to fuse with it as a sort of Claimed, or it returns as a being of spirit ephemera, hiding from discovery by Claiming human bodies rather than being able to possess Covers uniquely its own.<br /> <br /> Funny edge case: I'd probably allow it to work just fine if the demon was under the effects of Going Native when killed, and the Numen was used before the Embed expires. Reverts back to a demon when it runs out. If you set up a situation where you're able to make that happen in a narrow span of time, under great danger if anything goes wrong with your timing or ability to evoke the Numen from something, congratulations, you pulled some crazy bullshit, you can keep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:31:17-07:00","id":634684,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Raise Dead Exploit analogy, though I come to a different conclusion. I see no reason that Raise Dead can't work on a demon. It it couldn't, then the power would say that it can't work - most of the powers are good with saying when a demon can't use a power on another demon. Primum is the soul-analog of the demon and, while it doesn't move on like a true soul does, I see nothing that suggests that it has to instantly snuff out instead of slowly fading away. Kind of like recovering memory on a damaged computer system.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, its going to be rare for a demon to have the chance to use this power on a fellow demon. Generally, if a cult or an angel brings down a demon, then the body's going to be taken in for recycling. A fellow demon killing another demon is probably going to take steps to make sure that their fellow stays dead - there are powers to fake death, after all, so leaving a body around without being completely sure is a good way to get yourself killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-21-2015, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T09:50:36-07:00","id":635933,"title":"","content":"Based on the wording, I don't think a Demon would be resurrected as a Stigmatic, nor a Changeling as a Fae-Touched, etc. The resurrected character loses their powers, and Werewolves and Mages specifically come back as Wolf-Blooded and Sleepwalkers (which isn't even the Minor Template for Mage), respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T04:59:05-07:00","id":636890,"title":"","content":"Ummm.... Sleepwalker is a &quot;minor template&quot; for mage (not really sure if that's an official category in 2e anymore, but I know what you mean). According to Dave's blog, sleepwalker is to ghoul, and proximi is to revenant. I personally don't agree with that association, but its what the Mage developer officially said, so yeah.<br /> <br /> Part of what I'm basing my call on, though, are Prometheans. The quashmal were the first to have the Resurrection Numina, and I think the current version is just an updated version of that old one. The Numina wouldn't work on those who've died twice - you only get one escape from death. I've always ran it that the Numina would work on Prometheans, since the Azoth never really snuffed out, and kept them from ever fully dying. And Prommies and Demons are rather close. Though, looking back at it now, and all the options and revisions, I'm not sure if its meant to work on Prommies. And part of the reason mages and wolves (and to sleepwalker/wolf-blood noted) is that this is only the fourth game, and we don't know if there will be &quot;minor templates&quot; for changeling, beast, etc, nor what form these will take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T09:12:04-07:00","id":637079,"title":"","content":"Changelings will have the Fae-touched, but I don't think that Beasts have a minor template. Unless of course you count Heroes which I really don't.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-the-fae-touched/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...e-fae-touched/</a><br /> <br /> Then again would the Beast's soul aka the Horror be considered more like a Prommie's Pyros or a Demon's Aether than a normal soul (basically something that just can't be snuffed out)? Geisters and Mummies don't even need this ability to come back cuz that's just something they already do. As for Hunters aren't they pretty much just mortal+ &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> So I guess what I'm saying is, what we need to figure out is How it would affect Beasts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 08-25-2015, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:46:48-07:00","id":638711,"title":"","content":"I guess that sums it up, there's no &quot;real&quot; answer to this.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think treating it like the Raise the Dead exploit would be the best possible outcome. At least that power is DtD specific and makes context in sense of the game's mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}